taskDescription = "Sort the array in ascending order using insertion sort. Build the sorted array one element at a time by repeatedly taking the next unsorted element and inserting it into its correct position among the previously sorted elements."
taskName = "Insertion Sort"
taskGuide = "Big O Notation:
- Time Complexity: O(n²) worst and average cases, O(n) best case (already sorted)
- Space Complexity: O(1) - sorts in place

Use Cases:
- Small datasets (typically n < 50)
- Nearly sorted or partially sorted data - very efficient
- Online sorting - can sort data as it arrives
- When stability is required (maintains relative order of equal elements)
- Adaptive algorithm - performs well on data with existing order

Suitable Data Structures:
- Arrays and linked lists
- Works particularly well with linked lists due to insertion efficiency
- Any collection of comparable elements

Algorithm Steps:

1. Conceptually divide the array into two parts:
   - Sorted portion: starts with just the first element (index 0)
   - Unsorted portion: everything else

2. For each element in the unsorted portion:
   - This is your \"key\" element to be inserted
   - It needs to find its correct position in the sorted portion

3. Compare the key with elements in the sorted portion:
   - Start from the rightmost element of the sorted portion
   - Move leftward, comparing the key with each element

4. While the key is smaller than the comparison element:
   - Use swap(j-1, j) to shift the larger element one position right
   - Move to the next position left
   - Continue until you find where the key belongs

5. The key is now in its correct position:
   - All elements to its left are smaller or equal
   - All elements to its right (in the sorted portion) are larger

6. Expand the sorted portion by one element and repeat:
   - Continue until all elements are in the sorted portion
   - Call commitSort() when the entire array is sorted

Key Insight:
Like sorting playing cards in your hand - you pick up one card at a time and insert it into its correct position among the cards you're already holding."
exampleCode = "# Insertion sort
for i in range(1, len(array)):
    j = i
    while j > 0 and array[lb]j - 1[rb] > array[lb]j[rb]:
        swap(j - 1, j)
        j -= 1
commitSort()"
